grund guide — how to set up and use grund, one section at a time.

Usage:  grund guide [SECTION | --full]

With no argument it prints the front page: the three commands a fresh repository
runs, then every section with its size and what it holds. A fresh repository
needs only that; adopting grund in any other one reads `setup` next.

Arguments:
  SECTION  print one section, e.g. grund guide setup

Options:
  --full   print every section, `setup` first: the whole guide at once
           e.g. grund guide --full | less

Sections, in --full order:
  setup, config, citations, languages, members, scoped-guidance, schema, queries, editor, integrations, rules

The text is the Markdown shipped as `skills/grund-init/`: `SKILL.md` is the
`setup` section and `references/<name>.md` each other one. It is embedded in the
binary so installed agents can discover the setup workflow without the source tree.

Exit:  0 printed · 2 unknown section, unknown flag, or other CLI error.

Examples:
  grund guide                # the front page: fresh path, then every section
  grund guide setup          # adopting grund in a repository that is not fresh
  grund guide rules          # one reference section
  grund guide --full | less  # the whole guide, a page at a time
